1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
What was it like for you, for those
who may be experiencing that now,

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,500
discovering that your child was autistic?

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,000
By the time he was diagnosed,
I was already aware

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,500
something was wrong.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,500
So it was me begging
for a written diagnosis

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,000
in order for me to access
early intervention.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,500
I had to beg for a written diagnosis.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Because by the time he was two,

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,500
I'm like, my son should be talking.

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
I had three other kids before him.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,500
And his doctor was like,
"Just wait it out."

12
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,500
"Every kid is different."

13
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,000
But I still felt
something wasn't right.

14
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,500
So I started on my own
putting him in speech therapy

15
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,500
and things that I would look up to see

16
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,000
if that is what's wrong with my son,
what should I do?

17
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Speech therapy, occupational therapy.

18
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,500
But in that time I was told
about the regional center,

19
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,500
which is where we in California go

20
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,000
to access supports and services
for our children

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,500
and young adults on the spectrum
and with disabilities.

22
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:18,500
And in order to access
the early intervention,

23
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:22,000
I needed to have a diagnosis

24
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
before he was three years old.
